From: prplMesh virtual-radio lab
Subject: [PATCH] controller: reconstruct unassociated metric timestamp

The EasyMesh Unassociated STA Link Metrics response carries measurement age in
milliseconds, not an epoch timestamp.  The controller treated that age as
time_t seconds, producing dates near 1970 in NBAPI.  Reconstruct the
measurement time from the receipt clock and the reported age so consumers can
make a valid freshness decision.

This is protocol-data handling and applies to physical as well as simulated
radios.

--- a/controller/src/beerocks/master/tasks/link_metrics_task.cpp
+++ b/controller/src/beerocks/master/tasks/link_metrics_task.cpp
@@ -443,9 +443,13 @@ bool LinkMetricsTask::handle_unassociated_sta_link_metrics_response(
             UnassociatedStation::Stats stats;
             stats.uplink_rcpi_dbm_enc = sta_metrics.uplink_rcpi_dbm_enc;
 
-            time_t received_time = sta_metrics.measurement_to_report_delta_msec;
+            auto measurement_time =
+                std::chrono::system_clock::now() -
+                std::chrono::milliseconds(sta_metrics.measurement_to_report_delta_msec);
+            time_t measurement_time_t =
+                std::chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(measurement_time);
             char buf[sizeof "2011-10-08T07:07:09Z"];
-            strftime(buf, sizeof buf, "%FT%TZ", gmtime(&received_time));
+            strftime(buf, sizeof buf, "%FT%TZ", gmtime(&measurement_time_t));
             stats.time_stamp = buf;
 
             database.update_unassociated_station_stats(sta_metrics.sta_mac, stats, radio->dm_path);
